      "artist": "Jim Champion",
      "description": "Sea-worn granite boulders exposed by low tide, Nanjizal bay These boulders at the foot of the cliffs have been rounded and smoothed by the action of the sea over hundreds of years. Here they are exposed by the low tide, and their surfaces are slippery with seaweed. On the other side of the beach is Higher Bosistow Cliff and the chasm of Zawn Pyg.coa",
